      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Washington?",
      "a": "Washington receives $175M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The FY2027 to date total comes from 1,146 awards with an average award size of $153K, and obligations fell 99.1% year over year. By comparison, prior fiscal years show much higher totals, for example $19.4B in FY26 and $15.8B in FY25."
